menu "BTClock PoC LittleFS"

config BTCLOCK_LITTLEFS_SELFTEST
    bool "Run a boot-time LittleFS self-test"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the boot path writes a small file to the LittleFS
        partition, reads it back, asserts the contents match, and
        deletes it. Intended as a smoke test for the FS port — leave
        off in normal builds; flip on with `idf.py menuconfig` or set
        `CONFIG_BTCLOCK_LITTLEFS_SELFTEST=y` in
        `sdkconfig.defaults.<variant>` when bringing up a new board
        or partition layout.

endmenu
